<h1>nearest neighbor</h1>
<p>
(classic problem)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
Find the point (rectangle, line, etc.) that is closest to another point.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="spatialAccessMethod.html"><em>spatial access method</em></a>, <a href="pointAccessMethod.html"><em>point access method</em></a>.
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
<h2>Implementation</h2>
<a href="https://algorist.com/problems/Nearest_Neighbor_Search.html" target="_blank">(C, C++, and Java)</a>
<h2>More information</h2>
<p>
A <a href="http://mathworld.wolfram.com/VoronoiDiagram.html" target="_blank">Voronoi diagram</a> divides a plane into regions of nearest neighbors.
</p>

<hr>

Go to the
<a href="https://www.nist.gov/dads/">Dictionary of Algorithms and Data
Structures</a> home page.

<hr>

